## Volumes

- 01 - The Great Conversation
- 02 - Synopicon (Part 1)
- 03 - Synopicon (Part 2)
- 04 - Homer (800 BC)
- 05 - Aeschylus, Sophocles, Euripides, Aristophanes (525-385 BC)
- 06 - Herodotus, Thucydides (485-460 BC)
- 07 - [[Plato]] (ca. 427-347 BC)
- 08-09 - Aristotile (384-322 BC)
- 10 - Hippocrates Galen (460-201 BC)
- 11 - Euclid, Archimedes, Apollonius, Nicomachus (300 - 190 BC)
- 29 - Cervantes (1547-1616 AD)
- 30 - Bacon (1561-1626 AD)
- 52 - Dostoevsky (1821-1881 AD)
- 53 - James (1842 - 1910 AD)
- 54 - Freud (1856 - 1939 AD)

## Adler's Syntopion

Two volume index of the Encyclopaedia Britannica's Collection of Great Books of the Western World (GBBW). Serves as an index of 102 Great Ideas from the West listed alphabetically, from A to Z, 'Angel' to 'World'.

Under each heading and idea, serves as an introduction regarding each idea, and an outline of the core questions within each idea. Adler noted that the fundamental problem this project solves is that "different authors say the same thing in different way, or use the say words to say quite different things". The ambiguity in terminology makes approaching GBWW less accessible, and it is difficult to get a holistic view regarding Western thought. The Syntopion serves as a guide for holistic liberal education.

### Index

- Angel
- Animal
- Aristocracy
- Art
- Astronomy
- Beauty
- Being
- Cause
- Chance
- Change
- Citizen
- Constitution
- Courage
- Custom and Convention
- Definition
- Democracy
- Desire
- Dialectic
- Duty
- Education
- Element
- Emotion
- Eternity

